To determine if a string can be rearranged into a palindrome, we need to check the frequency of each character. A valid palindrome can have at most one character with an odd frequency, which would be placed in the middle. All other characters must have even frequencies.

The function `can_form_palindrome` uses a dictionary to count each character's occurrences. It then checks how many characters have odd frequencies. If the count of such characters is zero or one, the string can be rearranged into a palindrome.

